course: dictionary
lesson: 893
title: Birthright
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A birthright is something you have a right to just because of who you were born to be, such as your family, your country or your position. You do not earn it or buy it. «Freedom is our birthright» means every person is born with a right to freedom.
explain: In the Bible story, the birthright was the special share the eldest son got from his father. «Jacob tricked Esau out of his birthright and his father's blessing.» Esau was the older twin, so the birthright should have been his, but he gave it away for a bowl of stew.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Born and right are inside birthright, and tricked out of tells you something was taken away. So a birthright is something that belongs to you from birth.
fact: A birthright is something you have a right to just because you were born into a certain family, country or position.
fact: «Sell your birthright» means give up something precious that you were born to have, often for something small.
fact: In the Bible, the birthright was the special share the eldest son got from his father.
fact: Esau sold his birthright to his brother Jacob for a bowl of stew.
fact: «A birthright citizen» is someone who is a citizen from the moment they are born.
exercise: «Freedom is our birthright.» What is a birthright? | *Something you have a right to just because you were born | A trip to the seaside | A prize you win at school | A bowl of stew
exercise: In the Bible story, Esau sold his birthright for what? | A new coat | A horse | *A bowl of stew | A golden ring
exercise: «Jacob tricked Esau out of his birthright.» What does tricked out of mean here? | Made him laugh | Gave him a present | *Cheated him so he lost it | Helped him find it
test: «Every child's birthright is education.» What does this tell you? | Education is something you must buy | Only rich children can go to school | School is a kind of game | *Every child has a right to education just by being born
test: In the story, why was Esau's choice a bad one? | He was given a blessing by his father | He lost his bowl of stew | He won a race against Jacob | *He traded something precious for something small
exam: Ayo asks, «What is a birthright?» What is the best answer? | Something you must earn by working hard | A bowl of stew you are given for lunch | A prize for being the best at school | *Something you have a right to from birth, because of who you are born to be
